/// Magic Payments configuration.
///
/// ONE root, `payments`, and one key inside it. Which RAIL this build can serve
/// is deliberately NOT configured here: that answer comes from the conditional
/// import in the package's billing service factory, so a key claiming to enable
/// or disable Stripe or a store would be a SECOND answer to a question the
/// import graph already settles, and two answers eventually disagree. A
/// subscription bought on an iPhone is still managed in the App Store when the
/// customer opens the web app, and only the entitlement knows that.
Map<String, dynamic> get paymentsConfig => {
  'payments': {
    // Which driver PaymentsManager resolves. `platform` defers to the
    // conditional-import factory, which is what an app wants unless it
    // registered a driver of its own through `Payments.extend(name, factory)`.
    'driver': 'platform',
  },
};
